{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"lionly-squarish-xantus","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\n\n`unlink_core` (`src/rebar/_commands/unlink.py`) resolves both endpoints with `resolve_ticket_id` and raises \"Error: ticket '<x>' does not exist\" when the target does not resolve. A LINK whose stored `target_id` is not a ticket id therefore cannot be removed with `rebar unlink`. `rebar doctor`'s link repair walks only blocking relations (`_blocking_edges` in `src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py`), so it does not reach a dangling `caused_by`.\n\nLive instance: frank-rocky-rat (d52f-823f-894e-499a) holds LINK ceae9de7-8992-47c2-855c-60825331adc3, `caused_by` -> `6ed2`, written by the close-path bug surprising-fruticose-herring. `6ed2` matches 2 tickets, so `rebar unlink frank-rocky-rat 6ed2 caused_by` cannot address it. The remaining door is `rebar store maintenance`, a human-only break-glass path.\n\n## Impact\n\nDangling edges written before surprising-fruticose-herring's fix stay in the store and keep counting in the escaped-defect lenses. Agents cannot clear them.\n\n## Not yet checked\n\nHow many other tickets hold LINK events whose `target_id` does not resolve to exactly 1 ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A supported command removes a net-active link whose stored `target_id` does not resolve, addressed by the stored target string or by link uuid. A unit test drives a `caused_by` link with an ambiguous 4-hex target through it.","id":"ab5b-2942-6eaf-442f","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"No supported command removes a link whose target_id does not resolve to a ticket"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793699138270118001,"uuid":"04a8aa32-13fb-4659-9856-064ace744e32"}